/-!
# The affine line, `𝔾ₘ`, and the model purity

The rank-one computation that the whole of smooth purity rests on. The base `Y` is separated
of finite type over a field `k`, the coefficient ring `Λ` is finite with exponent invertible
on `Y`, and `p : 𝔸¹_Y → Y` is the projection, `s : Y → 𝔸¹_Y` the zero section and
`j : 𝔾_{m,Y} → 𝔸¹_Y` the open complement:

* the affine line is acyclic, `Λ_Y ≅ Rp_* Λ`, and `Rπ_* Λ(1)` has `Λ_Y(1)` in degree zero,
  `Λ_Y` in degree one, generated by the Kummer class `κ(t)`, and nothing else
  (`sk-prop-a1-kummer`);
* consequently the *fundamental class* `pur_s : Λ ≅ Rs^! Λ(1)[2]` of the zero section, the
  adjoint of the Kummer boundary `∂κ(t)` (`sk-prop-a1`);
* a complex on `𝔸¹_Y` that is a pullback is determined by its restriction to `t = 1`, so its
  fibres at `t = 0` and `t = 1` agree (`sk-prop-a1-inv`);
* iterating the one-dimensional case gives the model purity for `𝔸^c_B` (`sk-prop-an`), in two
  forms: the Thom class `th : Λ ≅ Rz^! Λ(c)[2c]` of the zero section `z`, and
  `Rπ^! K ≅ Lπ^* K(c)[2c]` for the projection `π`.

The invertibility hypothesis is not decorative: for `Λ = ℤ/p` over a base of characteristic
`p` the Artin–Schreier sequence gives `H¹(𝔸¹_k, ℤ/p) = k[t]/(F − 1)k[t] ≠ 0`, so the affine
line is not acyclic and every statement below fails.

## Implementation notes

Each clause that the blueprint states about a specific map is stated here as `IsIso` of that
map, defined in this file:

* `sk-prop-a1-kummer`: the unit map `Λ_Y ⟶ Rp_* Λ` (`affineLineUnit`), the map
  `π^* : Λ_Y(1) ⟶ Rπ_* Λ(1)` (`multiplicativeGroupDegreeZeroMap`) and the Kummer class map
  `Λ_Y ⟶ (Rπ_* Λ(1))[1]` (`multiplicativeGroupDegreeOneMap`). `𝔾_{m,Y}` is the open
  subscheme `D(t)` of `𝔸¹_Y` (`multiplicativeGroupOpen`).
* `sk-prop-a1`: the fundamental class `pur_s`, the adjoint of the Kummer boundary `∂κ(t)`.
* `sk-prop-an` (i): the Thom class `th`, the adjoint of `∂κ(t₁) ∪ ⋯ ∪ ∂κ(t_c)`
  (`affineSpaceThomClass`).

The Kummer classes are the concrete ones of `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.kummerClass`, built from
the Kummer sequence, so `sk-prop-a1` is a theorem about them
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.isIso_supportedClassMap_kummerBoundary_coord`), to be derived from
`sk-prop-a1-kummer` as in the blueprint. The zero sections are the closed subschemes `V(t)` cut
out by the coordinates; their identification with the base through `AffineSpace.zeroSection` is
not formalised.

Still stated only as existence, or not at all:

* `sk-prop-a1-inv` (ii) is stated in two halves: uniqueness of a comparison normalized at
  `t = 1`, and gluing of étale-local comparisons, the latter with local isomorphisms that are
  not required to be normalized (they can always be renormalized).
* `sk-prop-an` (ii), the `Rπ^!`-form, is stated as existence of an isomorphism: the comparison
  `γ_{π,K}` is the transpose of the trace, which for `c > 1` needs the composition isomorphism
  of `Rf_!`. The normalization (iii) is not stated, for the same reason. The vector-bundle form
  is stated for the normal bundle of a section only, in
  `WeilConjectures.EtaleCohomology.Purity.Smooth.Deformation`.

## Main definitions

- `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.multiplicativeGroupOpen`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.multiplicativeGroupProj`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.affineLineUnit`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.multiplicativeGroupDegreeZeroMap`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.multiplicativeGroupDegreeOneMap`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.affineSpaceThomClass`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.oneSectionLeftDerivedUpperStarIso`

## Main statements

- `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.isIso_affineLineUnit`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.isIso_homology_zero_map_multiplicativeGroupDegreeZeroMap`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.isIso_homology_zero_map_multiplicativeGroupDegreeOneMap`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.isZero_homology_rightDerivedLowerStar_multiplicativeGroup`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.isIso_supportedClassMap_kummerBoundary_coord`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.injective_upperStar_map_of_isFiniteLocallyConstantSheaf`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.injective_upperStar_oneSection_map_of_isFiniteLocallyConstantSheaf`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.eq_of_leftDerivedUpperStar_oneSection_eq`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.exists_iso_leftDerivedUpperStar_of_locally`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.isIso_affineSpaceThomClass`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.nonempty_iso_rightDerivedUpperShriek_affineSpace`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.nonempty_iso_dualizingComplex_affineSpace`
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory Limits MonoidalCategory

open scoped CategoryTheory.Functor

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

open Scheme

namespace Etale

variable (Λ : Type (u + 1)) [CommRing Λ] [Finite Λ]

section

variable {Y : Scheme.{u}} [HasInvertibleExponent Λ Y]

variable {G : Scheme.{u}} (j : G ⟶ 𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y)) [IsOpenImmersion j]

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-a1-inv`: Weak `𝔸¹`-invariance

*Uniqueness for lisse sheaf maps on `𝔸¹_Y`.* Two morphisms between finite locally constant
sheaves on `𝔸¹_Y` that agree after restriction to the open complement `G = 𝔾_{m,Y}` of the
zero section agree everywhere: the internal Hom is again finite locally constant, a section of
a locally constant sheaf on a connected scheme is determined by one geometric stalk, and every
connected component of `𝔸¹_Y` meets `𝔾_{m,Y}`. -/
theorem injective_upperStar_map_of_isFiniteLocallyConstantSheaf
    (hj : Set.range j.base = (Set.range (AffineSpace.zeroSection (ULift.{u} (Fin 1)) Y).base)ᶜ)
    (L M : Sheaf 𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y).smallEtaleTopology (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ))
    [Scheme.IsLocallyConstantSheaf L] [Scheme.IsFiniteSheaf L]
    [Scheme.IsLocallyConstantSheaf M] [Scheme.IsFiniteSheaf M] :
    Function.Injective fun φ : L ⟶ M ↦ ((j)^*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ]).map φ :=
  sorry

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-a1-inv`: Weak `𝔸¹`-invariance

*Uniqueness for lisse sheaf maps on `𝔾_{m,Y}`.* Two morphisms between finite locally constant
sheaves on `𝔾_{m,Y}` that agree after restriction along the unit section `i₁ : Y ⟶ 𝔾_{m,Y}`
agree everywhere. This is the second assertion of clause (i), and it is what `sk-thm-dnc`
Step 2 and `sk-prop-an` Step 3 use. -/
theorem injective_upperStar_oneSection_map_of_isFiniteLocallyConstantSheaf
    (hj : Set.range j.base = (Set.range (AffineSpace.zeroSection (ULift.{u} (Fin 1)) Y).base)ᶜ)
    (i₁ : Y ⟶ G) (hi₁ : i₁ ≫ j = AffineSpace.oneSection (ULift.{u} (Fin 1)) Y)
    (L M : Sheaf G.smallEtaleTopology (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ))
    [Scheme.IsLocallyConstantSheaf L] [Scheme.IsFiniteSheaf L]
    [Scheme.IsLocallyConstantSheaf M] [Scheme.IsFiniteSheaf M] :
    Function.Injective fun φ : L ⟶ M ↦ ((i₁)^*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ]).map φ :=
  sorry

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-a1-inv`: Weak `𝔸¹`-invariance

*Invariance along the line.* A comparison between an invertible complex `F` on `𝔸¹_Y` and a
pullback from `Y` is determined by its restriction to the unit section `t = 1`: two
isomorphisms `α, β : F ≅ Lp^* C` with `Li₁^* α = Li₁^* β` are equal. Consequently the
identifications `Li₀^* F ≅ C ≅ Li₁^* F` obtained from such a comparison are canonical, and the
invariant is *constant* along the `𝔸¹`-direction: its values at `t = 0` and at `t = 1` agree.

Invertibility of `F` is what puts the comparison inside the lisse rank-one world in which the
uniqueness statements above apply; it is the hypothesis `sk-prop-a1-inv` (ii) imposes, in the
weaker form available here (the blueprint asks that `F` be étale-locally a shift and twist of
a lisse rank-one sheaf). -/
theorem eq_of_leftDerivedUpperStar_oneSection_eq
    (F : _root_.DerivedCategory
      (Sheaf 𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y).smallEtaleTopology (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ)))
    (C : _root_.DerivedCategory (Sheaf Y.smallEtaleTopology (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ)))
    (hF : DerivedCategory.isInvertible Λ 𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y) F)
    (α β : F ≅ (L(((𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y) ↘ Y))^*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).obj C)
    (h : (L((AffineSpace.oneSection (ULift.{u} (Fin 1)) Y)^*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).map α.hom =
      (L((AffineSpace.oneSection (ULift.{u} (Fin 1)) Y)^*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).map β.hom) :
    α = β :=
  sorry

/-- The identification `Li₁^* Lp^* C ≅ C` of the restriction of a pullback to the unit section
`i₁ : Y ⟶ 𝔸¹_Y`, from `i₁ ≫ p = 𝟙 Y`. It is the normalization at `t = 1` of `sk-prop-a1-inv`
(ii). -/
noncomputable def oneSectionLeftDerivedUpperStarIso
    (C : _root_.DerivedCategory (Sheaf Y.smallEtaleTopology (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ))) :
    (L((AffineSpace.oneSection (ULift.{u} (Fin 1)) Y)^*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).obj
        ((L(((𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y) ↘ Y))^*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).obj C) ≅ C :=
  ((leftDerivedUpperStarComp (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ) (AffineSpace.oneSection (ULift.{u} (Fin 1)) Y)
      (𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y) ↘ Y) (𝟙 Y) (by simp)).app C).symm ≪≫
    (leftDerivedUpperStarId (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ) Y).app C

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-a1-inv`: Weak `𝔸¹`-invariance

*Invariance along the line, gluing half of clause (ii).* Let `F` be an invertible complex on
`𝔸¹_Y`, `C` a complex on `Y` and `φ : Li₁^* F ≅ C` an identification at the unit section. If
`F` is, étale-locally on `Y`, isomorphic to a pullback of `C`, that is, there are a jointly
surjective family of étale maps `e i : U i ⟶ Y` and isomorphisms
`F|_{𝔸¹_{U i}} ≅ Lp_i^* (C|_{U i})`, then there is a global isomorphism `κ : F ≅ Lp^* C`
normalized by `φ` at `t = 1`. By `eq_of_leftDerivedUpperStar_oneSection_eq` it is unique, so
`Li₀^* κ` is a canonical identification `Li₀^* F ≅ C ≅ Li₁^* F`.

The blueprint glues local isomorphisms that are already normalized at `t = 1`. The local
isomorphisms here are not normalized: any one can be corrected by the pullback of an
automorphism of `C|_{U i}`, and then the normalized local isomorphisms agree on overlaps by
uniqueness and glue, the étale-local sheaf `Hom(F, Lp^* C)` being concentrated in degree `0`
because `F` is invertible. The blueprint asks that `F` be étale-locally a shift and twist of a
lisse rank-one sheaf and that `F`, `C` be bounded constructible of finite Tor dimension; here
`F` is invertible and is assumed étale-locally isomorphic to a pullback of `C`. -/
theorem exists_iso_leftDerivedUpperStar_of_locally
    (F : _root_.DerivedCategory
      (Sheaf 𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y).smallEtaleTopology (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ)))
    (C : _root_.DerivedCategory (Sheaf Y.smallEtaleTopology (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ)))
    (hF : DerivedCategory.isInvertible Λ 𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y) F)
    (φ : (L((AffineSpace.oneSection (ULift.{u} (Fin 1)) Y)^*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).obj F ≅ C)
    {ι : Type u} {U : ι → Scheme.{u}} (e : ∀ i, U i ⟶ Y) [∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.Etale (e i)]
    (he : ⋃ i, Set.range (e i).base = Set.univ)
    (hloc : ∀ i, Nonempty
      ((L((AffineSpace.map (ULift.{u} (Fin 1)) (e i))^*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).obj F ≅
        (L(((𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); U i) ↘ U i))^*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).obj
          ((L((e i)^*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).obj C))) :
    ∃ κ : F ≅ (L(((𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y) ↘ Y))^*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).obj C,
      (L((AffineSpace.oneSection (ULift.{u} (Fin 1)) Y)^*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).mapIso κ ≪≫
        oneSectionLeftDerivedUpperStarIso Λ C = φ :=
  sorry

end

section

variable (Y : Scheme.{u})

/-- `𝔾_{m,Y}`, as the open subscheme of `𝔸¹_Y` on which the coordinate `t` is invertible
(`AffineSpace.multiplicativeGroupOpen`). -/
noncomputable abbrev multiplicativeGroupOpen : (𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y)).Opens :=
  AffineSpace.multiplicativeGroupOpen Y

/-- The projection `π : 𝔾_{m,Y} ⟶ Y` (`AffineSpace.multiplicativeGroupProj`). -/
noncomputable abbrev multiplicativeGroupProj : (multiplicativeGroupOpen Y).toScheme ⟶ Y :=
  AffineSpace.multiplicativeGroupProj Y

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-a1-kummer`: The affine line and `𝔾ₘ` with `Λ(1)`-coefficients

*The comparison for clause (a).* The map `Λ_Y ⟶ Rp_* Λ_{𝔸¹_Y}` for the projection
`p : 𝔸¹_Y ⟶ Y`: the unit of `Lp^* ⊣ Rp_*` at `Λ_Y`, followed by `Rp_*` of the unit comparison
`Lp^* Λ_Y ⟶ Λ_{𝔸¹_Y}` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.leftDerivedUpperStarUnit`). -/
noncomputable def affineLineUnit :
    constantComplex Λ Y ⟶
      (R((𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y) ↘ Y)_*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).obj
        (constantComplex Λ 𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y)) :=
  (derivedUpperStarLowerStarAdjunction (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ)
      (𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y) ↘ Y)).unit.app _ ≫
    (R((𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y) ↘ Y)_*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).map
      (leftDerivedUpperStarUnit (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ) (𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y) ↘ Y))

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-a1-kummer`: The affine line and `𝔾ₘ` with `Λ(1)`-coefficients

*Clause (a), acyclicity of the affine line*: `Λ_Y ⟶ Rp_* Λ` is an isomorphism, equivalently
`R^m p_* Λ = 0` for `m > 0` and `R⁰p_*Λ = Λ_Y`. On a geometric fibre it is the vanishing
`H^q(𝔸¹_k, μ_{ℓ^N}) = 0` for `q > 0`, from the Kummer sequence, the divisibility of `k^×` and
`Pic(𝔸¹_k) = 0`. -/
theorem isIso_affineLineUnit [HasInvertibleExponent Λ Y] : IsIso (affineLineUnit Λ Y) :=
  sorry

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-a1-kummer`: The affine line and `𝔾ₘ` with `Λ(1)`-coefficients

*The comparison for clause (b), degree zero.* The map `Λ_Y(1) ⟶ Rπ_* Λ_{𝔾_m}(1)`, `π^*`: the
unit of `Lπ^* ⊣ Rπ_*` at `Λ_Y(1)`, followed by `Rπ_*` of `Lπ^* Λ_Y(1) ≅ Λ_{𝔾_m}(1)`. -/
noncomputable def multiplicativeGroupDegreeZeroMap [HasInvertibleExponent Λ Y] :
    tateObject Λ Y 1 ⟶
      (R((multiplicativeGroupProj Y)_*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).obj
        (tateObject Λ (multiplicativeGroupOpen Y) 1) :=
  (derivedUpperStarLowerStarAdjunction (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ)
      (multiplicativeGroupProj Y)).unit.app _ ≫
    (R((multiplicativeGroupProj Y)_*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).map
      (leftDerivedUpperStarTateObjectIso (Λ := Λ) (multiplicativeGroupProj Y) 1).hom

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-a1-kummer`: The affine line and `𝔾ₘ` with `Λ(1)`-coefficients

*Clause (b), degree zero.* `π^* : Λ_Y(1) ⟶ R⁰π_* Λ(1)` is an isomorphism; on a geometric fibre
this is the Kummer computation `H⁰(𝔾_{m,k}, μ_n) = μ_n(k)`. -/
theorem isIso_homology_zero_map_multiplicativeGroupDegreeZeroMap [HasInvertibleExponent Λ Y] :
    IsIso ((_root_.DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor _ 0).map
      (multiplicativeGroupDegreeZeroMap Λ Y)) :=
  sorry

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-a1-kummer`: The affine line and `𝔾ₘ` with `Λ(1)`-coefficients

*Clause (c), vanishing above degree one.* `R^m π_* Λ(1) = 0` for `m ≥ 2`, by the cohomological
dimension of an affine curve. -/
theorem isZero_homology_rightDerivedLowerStar_multiplicativeGroup [HasInvertibleExponent Λ Y]
    (m : ℤ) (hm : 2 ≤ m) :
    IsZero ((_root_.DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor _ m).obj
      ((R((multiplicativeGroupProj Y)_*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).obj
        (tateObject Λ (multiplicativeGroupOpen Y) 1))) :=
  sorry

end

section

variable (c : ℕ) (B : Scheme.{u}) [HasCompactification (𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin c); B) ↘ B)]
  [HasInvertibleExponent Λ B]

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-an`: `𝔸¹ ⇒ 𝔸ⁿ`: the model purity

*Clause (ii), the `Rπ^!`-form: affine-space purity.* For the projection
`π : 𝔸^c_B ⟶ B` there is an isomorphism

`Rπ^! K ≅ (Lπ^* K)(c)[2c]`,

natural in `K ∈ D^b_{ctf}(B, Λ)`. In the blueprint it is the transpose `γ_{π,K}` under
`Rπ_! ⊣ Rπ^!` of the integration map `Rπ_! Lπ^* K(c)[2c] ≅ K ⊗^L Rπ_! Λ(c)[2c] ⟶ K`, built
from the trace `Rπ_! Λ(c)[2c] ≅ Λ_B` of the projective line and iterated along
`𝔸^c_B = 𝔸¹_{𝔸^{c-1}_B}`. This is the form of the model case that the rest of the chapter
uses: `sk-prop-cohsm` Step 1, `sk-lem-geometry` (4) and `sk-thm-smooth-purity` Step 3.

As for clause (i), `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.isIso_affineSpaceThomClass`, there is no field `k`
under `B`: the statement holds over any base on which
the exponent of `Λ` is invertible, as does smooth purity itself. -/
-- TODO(unify): sk-prop-an — state that the isomorphism is `γ_{π,K}`, compatible with base
-- change and with the composition law along `𝔸^{c+e}_B = 𝔸^c_{𝔸^e_B}`, once the projection map
-- and a canonical composition isomorphism for `R(-)^!` are available.
theorem nonempty_iso_rightDerivedUpperShriek_affineSpace :
    Nonempty ((DerivedCategory.constructibleFiniteTor (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ) B).ι ⋙
        rightDerivedUpperShriek (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ) (𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin c); B) ↘ B) ≅
      (DerivedCategory.constructibleFiniteTor (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ) B).ι ⋙
        L((𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin c); B) ↘ B)^*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ]) ⋙
          twistShift Λ 𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin c); B) c) :=
  sorry

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-an`: `𝔸¹ ⇒ 𝔸ⁿ`: the model purity

*Clause (ii) for the unit.* The dualizing complex of the projection `π : 𝔸^c_B ⟶ B` is

`ω_π = Rπ^! Λ_B ≅ Λ(c)[2c]`.

This is the case `K = Λ_B` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.nonempty_iso_rightDerivedUpperShriek_affineSpace`, and it is smooth
purity (`sk-thm-smooth-purity`) for `π`, in the same form as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.nonempty_iso_dualizingComplex_twistShift`. -/
theorem nonempty_iso_dualizingComplex_affineSpace :
    Nonempty (dualizingComplex (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ) (𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin c); B) ↘ B) ≅
      (twistShift Λ 𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin c); B) c).obj
        (constantComplex Λ 𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin c); B))) :=
  sorry

/- Blueprint `sk-prop-an`, clause (iii), the normalization, is not stated. It says that the
composite

  `Λ_B --th--> Rz^!(Λ(c)[2c]) --Rz^!(γ_{π,Λ})--> Rz^! Rπ^! Λ_B ≅ R(z ≫ π)^! Λ_B = Λ_B`

is the identity, where `th` is the Thom class of clause (i), `γ_{π,Λ}` the isomorphism of
clause (ii) and the last isomorphism the composition law for `z ≫ π = 𝟙 B`. It is an equation
between three specific morphisms. The Thom class is defined
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.affineSpaceThomClass`), and so is a composition isomorphism of
`R(-)^!` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.rightDerivedUpperShriekCompIso`, from the chosen composition
isomorphism of `Rf_!`), but `γ_{π,K}` is not: (ii) asserts only that *some* isomorphism exists,
because the rank-one trace `Rp_! Λ(1)[2] ⟶ Λ` it is the transpose of is not constructed. -/
-- TODO(unify): sk-prop-an — state clause (iii) once the trace and `γ_{π,K}` are defined.

end

end Etale

namespace Etale

variable (Λ : Type (u + 1)) [CommRing Λ]

section

variable (Y : Scheme.{u}) [HasInvertibleExponent Λ Y]

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-a1-kummer`: The affine line and `𝔾ₘ` with `Λ(1)`-coefficients

*The comparison for clause (b), degree one.* The map `Λ_Y ⟶ (Rπ_* Λ_{𝔾_m}(1))[1]` given by the
Kummer class `κ(t) ∈ H¹(𝔾_{m,Y}, Λ(1))` of the coordinate: the adjoint under `Lπ^* ⊣ Rπ_*` of
`Lπ^* Λ_Y ≅ Λ_{𝔾_m} ⟶ Λ_{𝔾_m}(1)[1]`. On `H⁰` it is the map `Λ_Y ⟶ R¹π_* Λ(1)`, `1 ↦ κ(t)`. -/
noncomputable def multiplicativeGroupDegreeOneMap :
    constantComplex Λ Y ⟶
      ((R((multiplicativeGroupProj Y)_*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).obj
        (tateObject Λ (multiplicativeGroupOpen Y) 1))⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧ :=
  haveI : HasInvertibleExponent Λ (multiplicativeGroupOpen Y) :=
    .of_hom (multiplicativeGroupProj Y)
  ((derivedUpperStarLowerStarAdjunction (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ) (multiplicativeGroupProj Y)).homEquiv
      _ _ ((leftDerivedUpperStarConstantComplexIso Λ (multiplicativeGroupProj Y)).hom ≫
        kummerClass Λ ((𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y)).basicOpenUnit
          (AffineSpace.coord Y (ULift.up 0))))) ≫
    ((R((multiplicativeGroupProj Y)_*[ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ])).commShiftIso (1 : ℤ)).hom.app _

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-a1-kummer`: The affine line and `𝔾ₘ` with `Λ(1)`-coefficients

*Clause (b), degree one.* `R¹π_* Λ(1)` is free of rank one on the Kummer class: the map
`Λ_Y ⟶ R¹π_* Λ(1)`, `1 ↦ κ(t)`, is an isomorphism. On a geometric fibre this is
`H¹(𝔾_{m,k}, μ_n) = ℤ/n`, generated by the class of `t`. -/
theorem isIso_homology_zero_map_multiplicativeGroupDegreeOneMap [Finite Λ] :
    IsIso ((_root_.DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor _ 0).map
      (multiplicativeGroupDegreeOneMap Λ Y)) :=
  sorry

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-a1`: Rank-one orientation: the fundamental class of the zero section

The fundamental class `pur_s : Λ_{V(t)} ⟶ Rs^!(Λ(1)[2])` of the zero section `s` of `𝔸¹_Y`,
the adjoint of the Kummer boundary `∂κ(t)` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.kummerBoundary`), is an
isomorphism. Here the zero section is the closed subscheme `V(t)` cut out by the coordinate.

This is the rank-one local calculation `H²_{0}(𝔸¹_ȳ, Λ(1)) ≅ Λ`, `∂κ(t) ↦ 1`; the blueprint
derives it from `sk-prop-a1-kummer` through the localization triangle of the zero section. It
pins down both the Kummer classes and the twisting object `Λ(1)`. -/
theorem isIso_supportedClassMap_kummerBoundary_coord [Finite Λ] :
    haveI : HasInvertibleExponent Λ 𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y) := .of_hom (𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y) ↘ Y)
    IsIso (supportedClassMap Λ (𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Y).zeroLocusSubschemeι
        {AffineSpace.coord Y (ULift.up 0)})
      (shiftSupportedClass (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ) _ 2
        (kummerBoundary Λ (AffineSpace.coord Y (ULift.up 0))))) :=
  sorry

end

section

variable (c : ℕ) (B : Scheme.{u}) [HasInvertibleExponent Λ B]

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-an`: `𝔸¹ ⇒ 𝔸ⁿ`: the model purity

*The Thom class of clause (i).* The adjoint
`th : Λ_{V(t)} ⟶ Rz^!(Λ(c)[2c])` of the cup product with supports
`∂κ(t₁) ∪ ⋯ ∪ ∂κ(t_c) ∈ H^{2c}_{V(t)}(𝔸^c_B, Λ(c))` of the Kummer boundaries of the coordinates
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.kummerBoundaryProduct`), where `z : V(t₁, …, t_c) ⟶ 𝔸^c_B` is the
zero section, as the closed subscheme cut out by the coordinates. -/
noncomputable def affineSpaceThomClass :
    constantComplex Λ ((𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin c); B)).zeroLocusSubscheme
        (Set.range fun k : Fin c ↦ AffineSpace.coord B (ULift.up k))) ⟶
      (R((𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin c); B)).zeroLocusSubschemeι
          (Set.range fun k : Fin c ↦ AffineSpace.coord B (ULift.up k)))^![ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ]).obj
        ((tateObject Λ 𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin c); B) c)⟦2 * (c : ℤ)⟧) :=
  haveI : HasInvertibleExponent Λ 𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin c); B) := .of_hom (𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin c); B) ↘ B)
  supportedClassMap Λ _
    (kummerBoundaryProduct Λ (fun k : Fin c ↦ AffineSpace.coord B (ULift.up k)))

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-an`: `𝔸¹ ⇒ 𝔸ⁿ`: the model purity

*Clause (i), the `Rz^!`-form.* The Thom class `th : Λ_{V(t)} ⟶ Rz^!(Λ(c)[2c])` is an isomorphism,
i.e. `Rz^! Λ_{𝔸^c_B} ≅ Λ(-c)[-2c]` with generator `∂κ(t₁) ∪ ⋯ ∪ ∂κ(t_c)`. The proof is an
induction on `c` through `𝔸^c_B = 𝔸¹_{𝔸^{c-1}_B}`, with `sk-prop-a1` over the base `𝔸^{c-1}_B`;
no relative Künneth formula for `Rz^!` is used, which for general constructible inputs is false.

The blueprint takes `B` separated of finite type over `k`; the statement holds over any base on
which the exponent of `Λ` is invertible. The identification of `V(t₁, …, t_c)` with `B` through
the zero section is not formalised. -/
theorem isIso_affineSpaceThomClass [Finite Λ] : IsIso (affineSpaceThomClass Λ c B) :=
  sorry

end

